{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the she-ass saw the angel of YHWH standing in the way.</b> This 'seeing' is a perception, not a seeing of the eye, for angels are not apprehended by the eyes of man, much less by the eyes of beasts, and it is unnecessary to say that it was not an intellectual seeing, for a beast has no intellect. Rather, the meaning of 'she saw' is that she sensed something frightening her and preventing her from passing, and she did not know what it was — for her apprehension did not extend to that; for if so, she ought to have said in her speech, 'An angel of YHWH stands before me with his sword drawn in his hand, and therefore I had to stop you.' Thus explained the Ramban, z\"l." "<b>And the she-ass turned aside from the way and walked in the field.</b> That wicked man had a great desire to curse Israel, for there is no man in the world who, seeing the signs he saw on the way, would not turn back — all the more so a diviner and soothsayer like him, whose entire craft was to meet omens. First, the she-ass turned from the straight path and veered toward the field — this is what it says, ״ותט האתון״. Second, ״ותלחץ אל הקיר״ — and she crushed against the wall, ״ותלחץ את רגל בלעם״ — and she crushed Balaam's foot; she alluded to him the nullification of his steps and the hindrance of his going, for the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, was not upon the intention in which he was going. Third, ״ותרבץ תחת בלעם״ — and she lay down under Balaam; she lay down beneath him and refused to go at all. All these were hints to him that YHWH had not chosen that path. Fourth, the great miracle that was performed through the speech of the she-ass; and here He explained to him that his intention was evil regarding the faculty of speech, and He informed him — who sets a mouth for man, or who makes mute — that the Holy One, blessed be He, can withhold speech from him and set it in the mouth of a beast; and therefore he has no cause to pride himself on the power of speech. Fifth, the matter was explained to him further, in order to nullify his going with the intention he had; and therefore the angel of YHWH revealed himself to him and said to him explicitly, ״הנה אנכי יצאתי לשטן״ — 'Behold, I have come out as an adversary,' because he was going with an evil intention, ״וירט הדרך״ — and he perverted the way. For the Holy One, blessed be He, had told him to go on the way on condition that he not curse — this is what it says, ״קום לך אתם״ — but he perverted the way, that is, skewed the path and went against Me. And after all this, He mentioned that he should turn back from the way — this is what it says, ״לא ידעתי כי אתה נצב לקראתי בדרך ועתה אם רע בעיניך אשובה לי״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The phrase וירט הדרך is translated hyper-literally following R. Bahya's own gloss ('עיות הדרך'); the root י-ר-ט is rare and possibly Aramaic, rendered here as 'perverted/skewed the way' per his explanation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:14.945174696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}